.TH PRISM 1 "" "PRISM" "PRISM Manual"
.SH NAME
prism \- review and safely merge AWS CodeCommit pull requests from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prism
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B prism run
.I pr_id
.RB [ \-\-path
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-repo
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-merge ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prism
runs the same review, description and merge pipeline as the PRISM desktop
application, with the same safety checks, but needs no display. Use it locally,
or ssh into the machine that has AWS access and the reviewer engine and review
from anywhere.
.PP
.B prism run
works out what it needs from the folder you are in: the git repository (from
any subdirectory), the CodeCommit repository name and region from its
.B origin
remote, then your saved defaults. A folder that holds several clones needs
.BR \-\-repo ;
PRISM never guesses between them.
.PP
Every run keeps a record and a log under
.IR ~/.prism/cli\-jobs/ ,
which is how the desktop application lists, stops and retries jobs started here.
The packaged desktop build accepts the same commands, for example
.BR "PRISM run 214" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "run " pr_id
Review pull request
.IR pr_id .
Runs in the foreground; Ctrl\-C stops it cleanly (twice to leave at once).
.TP
.B jobs
List running jobs.
.TP
.BI "logs " id
Show a job's transcript.
.TP
.BI "stop " id
Stop a running job.
.TP
.BI "retry " id
Run a finished job again with the same settings.
.TP
.BI "ask " "id question"
Ask the reviewer about a finished job. Read\-only: nothing is changed or merged.
.TP
.BI "rm " id ...
Delete finished jobs' records and logs.
.TP
.B models
List the reviewer models available.
.TP
.B repos
Show the git clones PRISM finds in a folder.
.TP
.B config
Show or change saved defaults.
.TP
.B update
Check for a newer release.
.TP
.B man
Install this manual page.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.B help
Show the built\-in command summary.
.SH OPTIONS FOR RUN
.TP
.BI \-\-path " DIR"
Project folder. Default: the git repository you are in, else the saved
.BR project_dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " NAME"
CodeCommit repository name. Default: saved
.BR repo ,
else the clone's remote, else the folder's name.
.TP
.BI \-\-clone " DIR"
Local clone to use when it is not the folder itself.
.TP
.BI \-\-region " REGION"
AWS region. Default: saved
.BR region ,
else the remote's region, else us\-east\-1.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Reviewer model; see
.BR "prism models" .
.TP
.BR \-\-review ", " \-\-no\-review
Run the review (default), or skip it and only sync and merge.
.TP
.BR \-\-describe ", " \-\-no\-describe
Write the findings into the PR description (default), or not. Always off
without a review.
.TP
.BR \-\-merge ", " \-\-no\-merge
Merge on approval (default), or review only.
.TP
.BR \-\-sync ", " \-\-no\-sync
Sync the destination branch into the source first (default), or not.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Review, but change nothing in AWS or git.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instructions " \fITEXT\fR"
Extra instructions for the reviewer.
.TP
.BI \-\-instructions\-file " FILE"
Read the extra instructions from a file.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detach
Run in the background and return; the job survives logging out.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print nothing. The log is still kept.
.PP
A flag always beats a saved default.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.B jobs \-a, \-\-all
Include finished jobs.
.TP
.B jobs \-\-json
Machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B logs \-f, \-\-follow
Keep following until the job ends.
.TP
.B logs \-n, \-\-lines \fIN\fR
Only the last N lines.
.TP
.B stop \-\-all
Stop every running CLI job.
.TP
.B retry \-d, \-q
Detach, or run quietly.
.TP
.B rm \-\-all
Delete every finished job.
.TP
.B models \-\-refresh
Ask the engine again instead of using the cached list.
.TP
.B update \-\-install
Download and install a newer release (packaged builds only).
.TP
.B man \-\-install, \-\-dir \fIDIR\fR, \-\-path
Install the manual page (default directory
.IR ~/.local/share/man/man1 ),
or print where it is.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Defaults live in
.I ~/.prism/config.json
(the file the desktop application also uses) under a
.B cli
key:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "cli": {
    "project_dir": "/home/me/work",
    "repo": "my\-service",
    "region": "eu\-west\-1",
    "model": "anthropic/claude\-sonnet\-5\-5",
    "instructions": "Flag missing tests",
    "review": true,
    "describe": true,
    "merge": false,
    "sync": true,
    "dry_run": false
  },
  "google_chat_webhook_url": "https://chat.googleapis.com/..."
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Text keys are
.BR project_dir ,
.BR repo ,
.BR region ,
.B model
and
.BR instructions ;
an empty value means "not set". Yes/no keys are
.BR review ,
.BR describe ,
.BR merge ,
.B sync
and
.BR dry_run .
Edit the file by hand or use:
.PP
.RS
.B prism config
.br
.B prism config set
.I key value
.br
.B prism config unset
.I key
.br
.B prism config path
.RE
.PP
The extra key
.B webhook
sets the Google Chat webhook shared with the desktop application.
.SH QUESTIONS
In a terminal, PRISM asks you directly when it needs an answer (merge conflicts,
the confirmation for a high\-impact merge). A detached or non\-interactive job
has nobody to ask and takes the cautious answer: conflicts are not resolved and
a high\-impact merge is not confirmed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Review PR 214 of the repository in the current folder:
.PP
.RS
prism run 214
.RE
.PP
Review only, without merging, in the background, then follow it:
.PP
.RS
prism run 214 \-\-no\-merge \-d
.br
prism logs 7f3a9c \-f
.RE
.PP
Set defaults once:
.PP
.RS
prism config set region eu\-west\-1
.br
prism config set model anthropic/claude\-sonnet\-5\-5
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (a finished review, merged or not).
.TP
.B 1
The job failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or the pull request is already being reviewed.
.TP
.B 130
The job was stopped.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.prism/config.json
Saved settings.
.TP
.I ~/.prism/cli\-jobs/
A record (\fIid\fR.json), log (\fIid\fR.log) and stop request (\fIid\fR.stop) per job.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns off coloured output.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README and docs/MANUAL.md in the PRISM repository.
